        ☐ Persistent scrolling COMBAT LOG (to-hit rolls, damage, effects) -- extend ScrollText
        ☐ Combat STATS counters -- PLAYER (left) vs MONSTER (right) columns showing
          # CRITS / # FUMBLES / # MAX DAMAGE / TOTAL DAMAGE.  [requested 2026-07-27]
          (chronicle already tracks g_crits/g_fumbles for the player; extend to the
          monster side + a max-damage tally + running total, drawn on the combat
          panel -- see DrawCombatPanel / DUNGEON! FX_* combat context.)
        ☐ Crit fanfare with narrated consequences ("entrails fly", "slammed prone", bonus
          damage shown: 1d8(+1) = 7 x2 = 14)
        ☐ Enemy + player PORTRAITS (ANSI art per monster / class)
        ☐ Colour-coded polyhedral dice tray (d20/d12/d10/d8/d6/d4) -- extend the tumbler
        This is the flagship consumer of the reusable engine's combat subsystem.

      sub-items below are done. Remaining chamber ambition (multi-pawn / a bigger
      Darkest-Dungeon presentation) folds into the DEEP TACTICAL COMBAT item.
        Per the manual, Dungeon! Rooms hold 1 monster + 1 treasure; CHAMBERS hold a
        3-monster gauntlet and NO treasure (only dropped loot), and allow multiple
          the hand-authored assets/data/chambers.txt (12 named halls; `chamberdump` verifies).
          ChamberEncounter (game/PLAY.bas) raises one monster per entry until CHM_DEAD = 3, and
          is_chamber makes ClaimTreasure grant no treasure, per the board-game rule.
          kind | name | weight | minlvl | maxlvl | text. Drawn with a weighted, depth-gated
          draw; mechanics keyed by `kind` in code (same idiom as traps/curios), everything
          else data. Kinds: gauntlet (the classic spawn), shrine (draws the curio deck),
          hazard (springs a trap), boon (potion or depth-scaled gold), lord (a boss-flagged
          guardian, +50% HP / +1 AC, and it DOES count as a grave).
          Rules preserved: a non-gauntlet event happens INSTEAD of a fight on that entry and
          the chamber still needs its 3 kills; at most ONE special event per chamber per run
          (CHM_EVDONE) so re-entering cannot farm boons. Validated by `dungeon.run datalint`
          (unknown kind, zero weight, impossible depth band, no gauntlet weight).

Doors:
